# Batch write-skip contract (`force_async`)

## Problem this prevents

When `batch_job_parameter.force_async=TRUE`, `AsyncItemWriter` passes a **`Future`** to `SkipListener.onSkipInWrite`, not writer type `O`. Fixing only one job mapper (e.g. booking) while leaving Vo mappers with redundant `unwrap()` — or a job-local `DpiBatchWriterSkipItemSupport` — duplicates platform logic and drifts on the next job.

## Single contract

| Layer | Owns | Must NOT |
|-------|------|----------|
| **platform-lib** `GenericListenerV3` | `BatchWriterSkipItemSupport.resolveSkipItem(item)` then `fromWriter(O)` | Cast `SkipListener<I,O>` on raw skip item |
| **Vo-typed mapper** (calc, billing, penal VO) | Null-safe field read on `O` | `Future`, `resolveSkipItem`, `DpiBatchWriterSkipItemSupport`, `unwrap()` |
| **List-typed mapper** (booking, interest posting) | `item == null \|\| item.isEmpty()` then `item.get(0)` | Future unwrap (listener already resolved) |

## DPI jobs (mandatory pairing)

All three use `GenericListenerV3` in `*BatchConfigService`:

- `dpiAccrualCalculation` → `DpiAccrualCalculationFailureEntityMapper` (`DpiAccrualCalculationVo`)
- `dpiAccrualBooking` → `DpiAccrualBookingFailureEntityMapper` (`List<DpiAccrualBookingVo>`)
- `dpiBilling` → `DpiBillingFailureEntityMapper` (`DpiBillingVo`)

After platform fix, **calc and billing mappers stay plain Vo mappers** — no async-specific code.

## Ship gate (automated)

When pending ship touches DPI batch mappers, `infra-batch` skip support, or `GenericListenerV3`:

```bash
bash scripts/bin/audit-batch-skip-mappers.sh --dpi-only   # DPI path
bash scripts/bin/audit-batch-skip-mappers.sh              # full accounting mappers
```

Wired in `scripts/bin/ship-loop-gate.sh`.

## Verify both async modes

```bash
ntest run dpic.batch.force_async_modes
```
